-- title:
--   Eichler orders of squarefree level form one genus
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb Q$ and let $q'$ be a prime number such that the quaternion algebra $\mathbb H=\left(\frac{a,b}{\mathbb Q}\right)$ satisfies `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt`: $a<0$, $b<0$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ the completed algebra $\mathbb H\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ has all its nonzero elements invertible exactly when $q'$ lies in $v$. Let $N$ be a nonzero squarefree natural number. Let $\Lambda,\Lambda'$ be $\mathbb Z$-submodules of $\mathbb H$ that are maximal orders, i.e. each contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, is finitely generated and spans $\mathbb H$ over $\mathbb Q$, and is not properly contained in another submodule with these four properties. Let $R,R'$ be Eichler orders of level $N$: each is an intersection $\Lambda_1\sqcap\Lambda_2$ of two maximal orders in which the relative index of its additive group in that of $\Lambda_1$ equals $N$. Assume $R\le\Lambda$ and $R'\le\Lambda'$. Then there is a unit $y$ of $\mathbb H\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb A_{\mathbb Q}^{f}$, where $\mathbb A_{\mathbb Q}^{f}$ is the finite adele ring of $\mathbb Q$, such that $\mathrm{conjByFiniteIdele}\,R'\,y=R$ and $\mathrm{conjByFiniteIdele}\,\Lambda'\,y=\Lambda$; here $\mathrm{conjByFiniteIdele}\,\Theta\,y$ denotes the $\mathbb Z$-submodule of those $x\in\mathbb H$ whose image in $\mathbb H\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb A_{\mathbb Q}^{f}$ lies in $y\,\widehat\Theta\,y^{-1}$, with $\widehat\Theta$ the additive subgroup generated by the elements $z\otimes\alpha$ for $z\in\Theta$ and $\alpha$ an everywhere-integral finite adele.
--
--   This is the one-genus statement for oriented Eichler orders of squarefree level in a definite quaternion algebra over $\mathbb Q$ ramified at a single finite prime: any two such pairs (Eichler order inside a maximal order) are conjugate by a single finite idele, equivalently locally conjugate at every finite place. It feeds the construction of explicit idelic conjugators used in the adelic description of the relevant quaternionic automorphic forms, being cited by [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsEichlerOrder.exists_conjByFiniteIdele_finiteIdeleDiagonal_mul_eq_of_squarefree_of_not_dvd_of_ne`](thm.html#QuaternionAlgebra.IsEichlerOrder.exists_conjByFiniteIdele_finiteIdeleDiagonal_mul_eq_of_squarefree_of_not_dvd_of_ne).
